Wednesday?\n\nLet me verify that. If he reads 20 on Monday, 12 on Tuesday, and 19 on Wednesday, then total is 20 + 12 + 19. Let me calculate that again: 20 + 12 is 32, plus 19 is 51. Yep, that adds up. So the answer should be 19.\n\nBut wait, the problem says he borrows 3 books on Monday. Does that mean that on Monday, he borrowed the first book, and then the second book on Tuesday, and the third on Wednesday? So the titles are on different days, and he borrows them each. So the numbers match. Therefore, the pages on Wednesday is indeed 19.\n\nWait, but hold on. Let me make sure there are no other factors here. The problem says he borrows 3 books on Monday. Then reads the first book with 20 pages, the second with 12, and then Wednesday. The total up to Wednesday is 51. So that is 20 + 12 + x = 51. So solving for x gives x = 51 - 20 -12 = 51 - 32 = 19. Yep, that's 19. Therefore, he read 19 pages on Wednesday.\n\nI don't think there's any trick here. It's straightforward arithmetic. The key is that the total pages on Monday and Tuesday add up to 32, so Wednesday adds 19. So the answer should be 19.\n</think>\n\nNico borrows 3 books from the library on Monday, reads 20 pages on Tuesday, and x pages on Wednesday (unknown). The total he read from Monday to Wednesday is 51 pages.\n\nWe are asked to find how many pages were read on Wednesday. The total number of pages from Monday to Wednesday is given by the equation:\n\n$$\n20 + 12 + x = 51\n$$\n\nSolving for $ x $, we get:\n\n$$\nx = 51 - 20 - 12 = 19\n$$\n\nTherefore, the number of pages he read on Wednesday is:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{19}\n$$<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Nico borrows 3 books from the library on Monday.  On Monday, he reads the first book with a total of 20 pages.  On Tuesday, he reads the second book with a total of 12 pages.  On Wednesday, he reads the third book.  If he has read a total of 51 pages from Monday to Wednesday, how many pages did he read on Wednesday?", "answer": "From Monday to Tuesday, Nico reads a total of 20 + 12 = <<20+12=32>>32 pages.\nOn Wednesday, he read a total of 51 - 32 = <<51-32=19>>19 pages.\n#### 19", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Nico borrows 3 books from the library on Monday.  On Monday, he reads the first book with a total of 20 pages.  On Tuesday, he reads the second book with a total of 12 pages.  On Wednesday, he reads the third book.  If he has read a total of 51 pages from Monday to Wednesday, how many pages did he read on Wednesday?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["19"], "solution": "19"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 74035, 31632, 1811, 220, 18, 6467, 504, 279, 6733, 389, 7014, 13, 220, 1913, 7014, 11, 566, 15804, 279, 1156, 2311, 448, 264, 2790, 315, 220, 17, 15, 6816, 13, 220, 1913, 7589, 11, 566, 15804, 279], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 752, 1430, 311, 975, 1526, 419, 3491, 3019, 553, 3019, 13, 2055, 11, 74035, 31632, 1811, 220, 18, 6467, 389, 7014, 13, 5005, 566, 15804, 1817, 2311, 448, 2155, 2150, 14579, 25, 220, 17, 15, 6816, 389, 7014, 11, 220, 16, 17, 6816, 389, 7589, 11, 323, 1221, 1045, 3311, 389, 7920, 13, 576, 2790, 6816, 1349, 504, 7014]}
