 increased the mileage to 30 miles per week. How many miles total did she run for the year?", "answer": "Each half of the year consists of 52 / 2 = <<52/2=26>>26 weeks.\nFor the first half of the year, Nicki ran a total of 20 * 26 = <<20*26=520>>520 miles.\nFor the second half of the year, Nicki ran a total of 30 * 26 = <<30*26=780>>780 miles.\nFor the entire year, Nicki ran a total of 520 + 780 = <<520+780=1300>>1,300 miles.\n#### 1300", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Nicki spent the last year running a lot. For the first half of the year, she ran a total of 20 miles per week. For the second half of the year, she increased the mileage to 30 miles per week. How many miles total did she run for the year?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["1300"], "solution": "1300"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 14991, 72, 7391, 279, 1537, 1042, 4303, 264, 2696, 13, 1752, 279, 1156, 4279, 315, 279, 1042, 11, 1340, 10613, 264, 2790, 315, 220, 17, 15, 8756, 817, 2003, 13, 1752, 279, 2086, 4279, 315, 279, 1042], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 594, 1490, 13, 14991, 72, 10613, 369, 279, 1156, 4279, 315, 279, 1042, 11, 892, 374, 220, 20, 5555, 11, 1290, 30, 9211, 279, 1156, 4279, 315, 279, 1042, 374, 220, 20, 5555, 13, 5005, 369, 279, 2086, 4279, 11, 892, 374, 1083, 220, 20, 5555, 13, 6771, 752, 7683, 429, 1112, 5512, 4279, 374, 4279, 279, 1042, 11]}
