or the first two rounds. So, each of these two rounds had 6 matches, so 6*2 = 12 matches. Then, the last round had 4 matches. He wins half of the 4 matches in the last round, so half of 4 is 2. Therefore total is 12 + 2 = 14. Therefore, the answer is 14. So, boxed 14. I think that's correct.\n\n**Final Answer**\n\\boxed{14}\n</think>\n\nTo determine how many matches Brendan won throughout the competition, we follow the problem's description step by step:\n\n1. Brendan wins **all** matches in the **first 2 rounds**, each of which had 6 matches. \n\n   Each round has 6 matches, so 2 rounds would have:\n   $$\n   6 \\text{ matches per round} \\times 2 \\text{ rounds} = 12 \\text{ matches}\n   $$\n\n2. The **last round** had 4 matches. Brendan won **half** of these matches:\n\n   $$\n   \\frac{4}{2} = 2 \\text{ matches}\n   $$\n\n   Therefore, in the last round, Brendan won **2 matches**.\n\n3. Adding the matches won in the first two rounds and the matches won in the last round, we find the total number of matches:\n\n   $$\n   12 \\text{ matches (first two rounds)} + 2 \\text{ matches (last round)} = 14 \\text{ matches}\n   $$\n\n---\n\nThus, Brendan won a total of $\\boxed{14}$ matches throughout the competition.<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Brendan has entered a kickboxing competition and wins matches against multiple contestants. He wins all of the matches in the first 2 rounds, each of which had 6 matches, then wins half of the 4 matches in the last round. How many matches did Brendan win throughout the competition?", "answer": "In the first 2 rounds, Brendan wins a total of 2 rounds * 6 matches per round = <<2*6=12>>12 matches.\nIn the last round, Brendan wins half of the matches which is 4 matches / 2 = <<4/2=2>>2 matches.\nThroughout the competition, Brendan has therefore won 12 + 2 = <<12+2=14>>14 matches.\n#### 14", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Bre